---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import type { Locale } from '../../i18n/config';
import { t } from '../../i18n/t';

interface Props {
  locale: Locale;
}

const { locale } = Astro.props;
---

<BaseLayout
  locale={locale}
  title={t(locale, 'terms.metaTitle')}
  description={t(locale, 'terms.description')}
  path="/terms"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-20 pt-10 sm:px-6 sm:pt-14" lang="en">
    <h1 class="text-[32px] font-medium leading-[1.05] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink sm:text-[44px]">
      {t(locale, 'terms.title')}
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-4 text-[16px] leading-[26px] text-body">{t(locale, 'terms.description')}</p>

    <div class="md-body mt-8">
      <p>
        JSON Bits is a free set of browser-based tools for working with JSON and nearby data formats.
        By using it you agree to the simple terms below. They exist to be read, not to trap you.
      </p>

      <h2>What the site provides</h2>
      <p>
        Every tool runs inside your own browser tab. You can paste text, drop a file, or open a file
        from your device, and the result is produced locally by a Web Worker. There are no accounts,
        no paid plans, and no uploads. The site is offered free of charge and may change over time.
      </p>

      <h2>Provided as is</h2>
      <p>
        The tools are provided “as is” and “as available”, without warranties of any kind, express
        or implied. We do not promise that a tool will be uninterrupted, error-free, or suitable for
        a particular purpose. Output is generated mechanically from the input you give it; always
        review a result before relying on it in production, a financial record, or any other context
        where a mistake would matter.
      </p>

      <h2>Your data and secrets</h2>
      <p>
        Although documents never leave your browser, you should still avoid pasting secrets,
        credentials, private keys, tokens, or personal data that you cannot risk exposing. Anything
        you paste is visible on your own screen, may be held in the tab's memory while a tool runs,
        and can be copied or downloaded by you. Closing the tab discards it. The site does not store
        document content, but it cannot protect you from your own clipboard or from someone looking
        at your screen.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>
        Use the site lawfully. Do not attempt to disrupt it, reverse-engineer it for harmful purposes,
        or use it to process data you have no right to handle. Because everything runs locally, most
        misuse would only affect your own device, but the spirit of this rule still applies.
      </p>

      <h2>Third-party services</h2>
      <p>
        The site intentionally uses no analytics, no advertising, and no third-party scripts. The
        hosting provider delivers static files and may log ordinary request metadata such as IP
        address and browser version. If advertising is added in the future, this page and the Privacy
        Policy will be updated before it appears.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms when the site changes. The date below records the last revision.
        Questions can be sent to the contact address published on the site's GitHub repository or
        project page; no account or support contract is implied.
      </p>
      <p>
        <time datetime="2026-11-23">Last updated 23 November 2026</time>
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
